TEXT 0 -704 Left 2 ;Problems 9.3 - 4th-order Linkwitz-Riley (slide 15) crossover at fc for Peerless SLS-P830669 (40 L closed box) + NE123W-08 midrange (2 L closed box)
TEXT 0 -672 Left 2 ;IMPEDANCE analogy: electrical V = voltage, I = current | mechanical V = force, I = velocity. Closed box: M_AB = M_A1 so M_MC = M_MS, and C_MT = C_MS/(1 + V_AS/V_B).  Filters designed on R_E.
TEXT 0 -608 Left 2 !.param Rew=5.6 Lew=0.00112 Blw=11.88 Mmsw=0.0741 Rmsw=2.0729 Cmsw=0.000345 Sdw=0.05228 Vasw=0.13242 Vbw=0.04 Cmtw={Cmsw/(1+Vasw/Vbw)}
TEXT 0 -576 Left 2 !.param Rem=6.27 Lem=6e-05 Blm=5.53 Mmsm=0.0047 Rmsm=0.36364 Cmsm=0.0014332 Sdm=0.00541 Vasm=0.00589 Vbm=0.002 Cmtm={Cmsm/(1+Vasm/Vbm)}
TEXT 0 -544 Left 2 !.param fc=250 pol=1
TEXT 0 -512 Left 2 !.param L1w={1.886*Rew/(2*pi*fc)} C1w={1.591/((2*pi*fc)*Rew)} L2w={0.943*Rew/(2*pi*fc)} C2w={0.354/((2*pi*fc)*Rew)} C1m={1/((2*pi*fc)*1.886*Rem)} L1m={Rem/((2*pi*fc)*1.591)} C2m={1/((2*pi*fc)*0.943*Rem)} L2m={Rem/((2*pi*fc)*0.354)}
TEXT 0 -448 Left 2 ;c) LR4 must be summed with the SAME polarity (pol=1); try fc = 300 or 350
TEXT 960 -176 Left 2 ;woofer: electrical loop (I(Vdw) = i)          mechanical loop (I(Vmw) = u)
TEXT 928 304 Left 2 ;midrange: electrical loop (I(Vdm) = i)        mechanical loop (I(Vmm) = u)
TEXT 0 816 Left 2 ;the same two filters loaded by R_E only (what the textbook formulas assume): compare V(vw_id) with V(vw), V(vm_id) with V(vm)
TEXT 0 1264 Left 2 ;far field at 1 m: p = j w rho S_D u / (2 pi r)  ->  E = rho*S_D/(2 pi) * s on the velocity.  Sum p_tot = p_w + pol * p_m.  SPL in dB: plot V(pw)*5e4, V(pm)*5e4, V(ptot)*5e4
TEXT 0 1648 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 20 20k
TEXT 0 1696 Left 2 ;check: woofer |Z_E| peak 74 ohm at f_C = 65.4 Hz, midrange 90 ohm at 121.8 Hz.  Mid-band SPL at 2.83 V: woofer 92.1 dB, midrange 88.8 dB.  Z_in of a branch: V(in)/I(Vdw) is NOT it (the filter shunt draws current too)
